{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791118431,"nonce":"i8NuYKcFQpe/fRt1oShxWqIFqA8=","title":"system-ui should be SF Pro on macOS, which needs variable font weights","message":"Browsers resolve system-ui to SF Pro on macOS. Its only face there is /System/Library/Fonts/SFNS.ttf, a variable font with a wght axis. blinc_text has no font variation support, so every weight draws as the default, regular: headings, semibold labels and bold text all lose their weight.\n\nblinc_abi's SYSTEM_UI list (text.rs) names Helvetica Neue on macOS for now. Its static Regular, Medium and Bold faces work, and its metrics centre capitals in a CSS line box as SF Pro's do. Helvetica, which Blinc's generic sans-serif picks, sets them about 1.25px high at 14px, as AlignScene measured.\n\nTo do:\n- Blinc: apply the requested weight to variable faces, via ttf-parser's Face::set_variation for wght, in shaping and rasterizing. Hand this to the Blinc session.\n- ashui: once that lands, put \".SF NS\" back at the head of SYSTEM_UI and re-run tools/snapshot/scenes/AlignScene.hx and TypographyGallery.hx.","files":null}]}